5cqq|v|To fasten with a lock, or as with a lock; to make fast; to prevent free movement of; as, to lock a door, a carriage wheel, a river, etc. ; To prevent ingress or access to, or exit from, by fastening the lock or locks of; -- often with up; as, to lock or lock up, a house, jail, room, trunk. etc. ; To fasten in or out, or to make secure by means of, or as with, locks; to confine, or to shut in or out -- often with up; as, to lock one's self in a room; to lock up the prisoners; to lock up one's silver; to lock intruders out of the house; to lock money into a vault; to lock a child in one's arms; to lock a secret in one's breast. ; To link together; to clasp closely; as, to lock arms. ; To furnish with locks; also, to raise or lower (a boat) in a lock. ; To seize, as the sword arm of an antagonist, by turning the left arm around it, to disarm him. ; To become fast, as by means of a lock or by interlacing; as, the door locks close.	o:an50,65,1;1lt9,64,1;2a1h,63,1;4yxe,61,3;2zq7,59,94;75vj,56,3;9c4a,55,3;1lt8,50,4;9c4b,50,3;882h,49,1;1te9,45,88;8bdv,43,2;ipo,43,20;hpz,40,6;anw2,38,1~8ctd,11,560;9d84,4,227;2zq7,59,94;1te9,45,88;6pzw,10,74;33zs,16,54;3iwi,15,44;4fnz,3,32;11jd,10,21;ipo,43,20;9pp1,25,16;62qi,30,16;8td8,17,15;45ml,33,15;aft4,3,14	s:apxv,96,19;19qu,85,4858;1zi8,76,19;25kf,71,3;hq1,70,7;2zg,62,131;af5,60,5;7r87,54,1;7rgw,48,2;xyl,45,9;3y8d,42,12;7uhr,41,9;25o2,30,3;12wj,25,45;2lks,23,51~19qu,85,4858;2zg,62,131;2lks,23,51;aivw,19,50;12wj,25,45;7vqz,13,44;1suk,17,36;5ctj,8,31;apxv,96,19;67p,16,19;1zi8,76,19;6jxt,20,17;3y8d,42,12;2h0q,7,10;7uhr,41,9	d:724t,75,8;9n5p,70,67;9hcy,41,338;2qfy,33,5;5irf,32,7;32i4,32,98;4e6r,31,32;71cn,29,107;6ozn,28,2;3xbl,27,5;mcl,27,10;1zn,25,145;5oki,22,18;43yu,19,33;2rv7,18,197~oaz,11,399;1pwi,8,385;9hcy,41,338;2rv7,18,197;5jox,4,196;1zn,25,145;71cn,29,107;32i4,32,98;9n5p,70,67;881s,14,63;7wb2,14,42;43yu,19,33;4e6r,31,32;8exj,17,20;5oki,22,18	D:8u1o,29,6;64f5,26,1;4028,11,2~8u1o,29,6;4028,11,2;64f5,26,1
